DESIGN  (src/sync/)
  - Adb: blocking wrapper (program lookup: settings, PATH, ~/Android/Sdk,
    $ANDROID_HOME), devices -l, mdns services, connect, getprop, wlan0 address,
    listFiles, df, push/pull (paths passed as argv, no shell), mv/rm via quoted shell.
  - SyncPlan (pure, unit-tested): match by phone-side name (illegal chars → yt-dlp's
    full-width forms), size compare. Merge: new both ways; deleted-on-one-side is put
    back (keep olds); tombstoned-here → DeleteRemote. Mirror: uses the previous
    in-sync set to carry deletions; first sync never deletes. Same name, different
    size → Conflict, untouched, and excluded from the in-sync set (else a later mirror
    could delete one of two different files — caught by the test).
  - Collection schema v3: sync_state(device = ro.serialno, local_root, rel).
  - SyncSession: scan (worker) → Plan; run (worker) checked items only. Push to
    "<name>.cbpart" then mv; pull to "<name>.cbpart" then rename (refuses to
    overwrite a file that appeared meanwhile). DeleteLocal = Trash + tombstone.
    Sync state, tombstones and library rescan applied on the GUI thread before the
    dialog hears "finished". Cancellable between files.
  - Devices: polls `adb devices` every 10 s; identifies phones by ro.serialno so USB
    and Wi-Fi are the same phone; remembers model, last wlan0 IP, tcpip flag.
    Reconnect: mDNS _adb-tls-connect service whose name holds the serial (what
    worked for this phone before), then lastIp:5555 if tcpip was set up. "Set Up
    Wi-Fi Sync" (cabled): `adb tcpip 5555` + connect, until reboot.
  - UI: Sync Phone dialog (phone + state + Wi-Fi buttons, folder pairs editable,
    Merge/Mirror, Check → grouped checkable plan with sizes and reasons, free-space
    guard (keeps 512 MB), Sync with progress/cancel, confirmation listing deletions).
    Sidebar DEVICES lists phones (dim when remembered but offline); click → Sync.

